  "slug": "galaxy-clustering-cc66",
  "summary": "Eight preprints use simulations and mocks to size parameter biases from n(z), lens multipoles, light-cone effects and halo bias ahead of Euclid-class and DESI analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of simulations and mocks to quantify how astrophysical and modelling systematics propagate into cosmological inference. Euclid-like 3×2pt analyses show that n(z) errors bias w0wa, motivating on-the-fly Gaussian Process reconstruction. IllustrisTNG ellipticals show multipole mass terms bias time-delay H0 by 1–6%. Light-cone and relativistic effects shift local fNL by about 2σ (Euclid-like) and over 10σ (MegaMapper-like). On the bias side, TNG300 links halo secondary bias largely to unbound circum-halo matter, luminosity-weighted marked correlations are proposed as an assembly-bias null test on DESI-BGS mocks, and the hybrid Lagrangian expansion is extended to post-reconstruction clustering. Baryonification V produces tSZ Compton-y maps from dark-matter-only light cones. The DESI Legacy cluster test of general relativity is a more peripheral item.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
